  "notes": "The producer/engineer half of the benchmark 90s female-narrative-ballad sound. The entry calls his drum capture \"the single most complete in this file,\" and the part of it that reaches a note generator is the dynamic shape rather than the chain: the grammar is \"cross-stick verse into a hard 2&4 chorus\" with the \"Sky Hook\" compressed room mic fourteen feet above the kit producing the explosive chorus character — authored as a very wide accent-to-main velocity spread and room-driven fills into the final chorus. The stated signal-chain principle is a humanize fact, not a mix one: \"high-quality discrete preamps and compressors in front of tape, **minimal correction after**,\" so the timing stays played rather than gridded, and the bass is \"warm and analogue-tape-saturated\" root motion rather than a tight modern line. The session-culture note is authored as low fill variance and a maximal final chorus: \"the players approached the date with 'intention,' not as one of several dates that day — model deliberate, non-routine performances.\" ⚠ **No `progressionFamilies` are authored.** The entry names one tempo reading and no numerals at all, so the genre's families are inherited and only the extension spread, the voicing and the harmonic rhythm are authored — which is what \"two acoustics, a lead electric, pedal steel, keys, and sampled orchestra bells\" actually determines. ⚠ The signature production's ~117 reading is marked [LOW-CONF] in the research. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the velocity tiers, the humanize values, the perc density and the counter ratio.",
